# Watchmetrics

TV series analytics web app: search a show and see how ratings evolved episode-by-episode across IMDb, Rotten Tomatoes, and Metacritic.

## Stack

- **Backend**: Kotlin, Spring Boot 3, Gradle (Kotlin DSL)
- **Frontend**: Thymeleaf templates, HTMX, Tailwind CSS v4
- **Package**: `com.watchmetrics`

## Architecture (planned)

- Server-rendered pages with HTMX partial updates — no SPA framework
- External rating APIs / scrapers behind a service layer (not yet implemented)
- Charts and episode timelines added incrementally

## Current state

- [x] Project scaffold (Spring Boot, Thymeleaf, HTMX CDN, Tailwind build)
- [x] Home page placeholder at `/`
- [x] Series search (TMDB + HTMX live search at `/search`)
- [ ] Series detail page (ratings & charts)
- [ ] Rating data ingestion (IMDb / RT / Metacritic)
- [ ] Episode evolution charts

Update the checklist above as features land.

## Conventions

- Keep diffs small; match existing patterns before introducing new abstractions
- Prefer server-side rendering + HTMX over client-side JS frameworks
- Do not commit secrets (API keys go in env vars or local config, never in git)
